        <!-- The hexagons themselves are painted by three.js on the canvas behind this, the
             same way droparabia-official's HexBackground does it: one rounded-hex
             ShapeGeometry, a metallic gradient baked into its vertex colors, instanced under
             an orthographic camera mapped 1:1 to CSS pixels. CSS still owns the layout — the
             script just measures each cell and drops a hexagon behind it — so the text stays
             real text, selectable and readable by a screen reader.

             Each cell also carries a flat clip-path hexagon of its own, which is what shows
             if WebGL is unavailable; it's dropped the moment the canvas has actually drawn. -->
        <div class="hex-stage" id="hex-stage">
          <canvas class="hex-canvas" id="hex-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

          <ul class="hex-row">
